{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468149-advantages-flaws-v5","id":1468149,"title":"Advantages / Flaws v5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-17T10:15:41-08:00","id":1468149,"title":"Advantages / Flaws v5","content":"So, I'm working on a dhampir character, essentially building out a mortal and giving it some of the old pieces to make it fit - (Gets a Beast, has Potence and another Discipline at dot 1, etc.) and for the most part, this is working out great! <br /> <br /> I've ran into a hiccup - on the Companion creation book, which is how I'm building a mortal in the first place, it mentions that there are mortal-specific merits and flaws - but I've looked all through the core rulebook, the companion creation book, and a random quick reference pdf I found, and I just cannot find these mortal-specific merits and flaws. Further, the ones available in the book are almost universally about vampires (which makes sense, of course) but as dhampirs are just considered mortals, I can't actually figure out how most of these things apply to one. I was considering maybe doing some thin-blood merits / flaws, but that feels like a cop-out on my part. <br /> <br /> So, I was just hoping someone could point me in the right direction. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24203-venjamin","name":"Venjamin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:00:01-08:00","id":1468154,"title":"","content":"The merits/flaws in the Companion are in the Companion. p.59-60","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:08:42-08:00","id":1468156,"title":"","content":"There aren't any merits available only for mortals. \u200bI wouldn't consider Dhampir's just mortals though, and as they aren't in V5, if I were to include them I would just make them a Ghoul that doesn't require Vitae. Or Thinbloods.<br /> <br /> Also which meritis do you have questions about? You can't take a lot of them, and they are all pretty clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:38:49-08:00","id":1468161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468149-advantages-flaws-v5?p=1468154#post1468154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merits/flaws in the Companion are in the Companion. p.59-60</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, it only seemed to have ghoul-specific stuff, and the psychological pieces could be applied anywhere, so I was hoping there was a specific mortal-only. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468149-advantages-flaws-v5?p=1468156#post1468156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There aren't any merits available only for mortals. \u200bI wouldn't consider Dhampir's just mortals though, and as they aren't in V5, if I were to include them I would just make them a Ghoul that doesn't require Vitae. Or Thinbloods.<br /> <br /> Also which meritis do you have questions about? You can't take a lot of them, and they are all pretty clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately that's what I'm finding - the only reason I thought there were was that the companion book said there was. I guess that was my biggest concern is that most of the flaws are like, extreme? And don't necessarily fit the character in question. Same with the merits. I think I'm just going to put points in generic stuff and go from there and whatever's left over add to the group pool. It was just since there had to be flaws, and none of the flaws necessarily apply, I was worried about getting them to that point. <br /> <br /> I could probably mechanically do something with the Ghoul layout, since there's a vampire frenzy thing in there, but for now I'm pretty satisfied with the mechanics and how I got there, so it's all good. <br /> <br /> Thank you both for the clarification!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24203-venjamin","name":"Venjamin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:44:22-08:00","id":1468163,"title":"","content":"Some loresheets could apply depending on ST approval. But yeah the ghoul flaws in the companion are pretty bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T00:22:27-08:00","id":1468388,"title":"","content":"It might also make sense to invent some new Advantages? For example, dhampir myths often present them as being able to hunt down vampires. So you could have a Blood Hound Merit, which adds one die per dot to tests for tracking vampires of your parents' clan and half as many for tracking other vampires.<br /> <br /> Another folkloric benefit of dhampirs is that they have flexible bones, allowing them to squeeze under doors and through small gaps. You could rule that they could buy that as a five-dot Merit, Soft Bones.<br /> <br /> You could probably think of other things that are appropriate to add in, or add existing Merits, Backgrounds and Flaws (e.g., Unbondable might be appropriate in some cases).<br /> <br /> There are also lots of appropriate V20 Merits that might port over with a little bit of conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}